Backport of upstream gramps-web-api 99f5eff ("Fix OIDC login 500 for
disabled/unconfirmed accounts (negative roles)", PR #998, fixes #997,
2026-09-22).

Carried here because the fix is in upstream's git but not in any published
image: ghcr.io/gramps-project/grampsweb:latest was last rebuilt 2026-09-20,
two days before this landed, and that rebuild is the digest this image is
built FROM. Without it, get_permissions() raises KeyError for a negative role
and any account that is not auto-promoted by oidc-new-user-role.patch gets a
bare "Internal Server Error" instead of the "Account Under Review" page.

DELETE THIS FILE when the base image is bumped to a rebuild that includes it.
The build applies patches with --fuzz=0, so it will fail loudly rather than
silently double-apply.
index f143e9f..e8d27c1 100644
--- a/gramps_webapi/auth/const.py
+++ b/gramps_webapi/auth/const.py
@@ -129,6 +129,15 @@ PERMISSIONS[ROLE_ADMIN] = PERMISSIONS[ROLE_OWNER] | {
     PERM_DISABLE_TREE,
 }
 
+# Users with a negative role (disabled or unconfirmed) hold no permissions,
+# but the role must still be a key here: get_permissions() looks up
+# PERMISSIONS[user.role] directly, and the OIDC callback resolves permissions
+# before it checks for a disabled account, so a missing key raises instead of
+# reaching the "Account Under Review" page. Local login is unaffected (it
+# rejects a negative role before any permission lookup).
+PERMISSIONS[ROLE_DISABLED] = set()
+PERMISSIONS[ROLE_UNCONFIRMED] = set()
+
 # keys/values for user claims
 CLAIM_LIMITED_SCOPE = "limited_scope"
 SCOPE_RESET_PW = "reset_password"
